  "prefLabel": "Psyc 205.04 Roles of Board Staff and Complainants",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Psyc 205.04 Roles of Board Staff and Complainants.\n\n(a) Unless called as witnesses, board staff shall have no role in any enforcement or disciplinary hearing.\n\n(b) Unless called as a witness or granted party or intervener status, a person who initiates an adjudicative proceeding by complaining to the board about the conduct of a licensee shall have no role in any enforcement or disciplinary hearing regarding the licensee.\n\nSource. #12035-A, eff 11-4-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/psyc100-500.html"
